  "papers": {
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Latent Spatial Memory for Video World Models",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09828v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:59:54Z",
        "description": "Video world models that maintain 3D spatial consistency across generated frames typically rely on explicit point cloud memory constructed in RGB space. This design is both computationally expensive, requiring repeated rendering and VAE encoding, and inherently lossy, as the round trip through pixel ",
        "title_cn": "视频世界模型的潜伏空间记忆"
      },
      {
        "title": "MemoryVLA++: Temporal Modeling via Memory and Imagination in Vision-Language-Action Models",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09827v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:59:53Z",
        "description": "Temporal modeling is essential for robotic manipulation, as effective control requires both memory of past interactions and imagination of future states. However, most VLA models rely primarily on the current observation and therefore struggle with long-horizon, temporally dependent tasks. Cognitive",
        "title_cn": "MemoryVLA + + ：通过视觉-语言-动作模型中的记忆和想象力进行时间建模"
      },
      {
        "title": "AHA-WAM:Asynchronous Horizon-Adaptive World-Action Modeling with Observation-Guided Context Routing",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09811v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:55:18Z",
        "description": "World-action models have emerged as a promising paradigm for robot manipulation, jointly modeling visual scene dynamics and actions to inject physical priors into policy learning. However, existing world-action models couple world prediction and action execution at the same temporal resolution, forc",
        "title_cn": "AHA-WAM ：具有观察引导上下文路由的异步水平自适应世界动作建模"
      },
      {
        "title": "Universal Suppression of Gravitational Waves from Black Hole Evaporation Dynamics",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09804v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:54:14Z",
        "description": "Evaporating black holes can leave distinct imprints on gravitational wave (GW) backgrounds. We show that black hole populations with finite width mass distributions exhibit a universal late time evolution governed by the evaporation dynamics rather than the details of the initial mass distribution, ",
        "title_cn": "黑洞蒸发动力学引力波的通用抑制"
      },
      {
        "title": "SIGA: Self-Evolving Coding-Agent Adapters for Scientific Simulation",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09774v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:35:17Z",
        "description": "Advanced scientific simulators expose specialized input languages that turn simulation goals into executable configurations, but learning them can cost domain scientists hours to days. We study simulator setup as a problem of agent-tool interface grounding: what minimal simulator-specific adaptation",
        "title_cn": "SIGA ：用于科学模拟的自进化编码代理适配器"
      },
      {
        "title": "RPA as a Hessian Closure: Effective Functionals and Source-Variable Duality Across DFT, LR-TDDFT, 1RDMFT, and MBPT",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09763v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:26:30Z",
        "description": "We present a variational formulation of the random phase approximation (RPA) that places density functional theory (DFT), linear-response time-dependent density functional theory (LR-TDDFT), one-body reduced density matrix functional theory (1RDMFT), and Green's function many-body perturbation theor",
        "title_cn": "RPA作为黑森闭包：跨DFT、LR-TDDFT、1RDMFT和MBPT的有效函数和源变量二元性"
      },
      {
        "title": "bbsolver: A Unified Error-Bounded Spatiotemporal Optimization Solver for Key Timing and Topology-Consistent Vector Paths",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09741v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T17:04:33Z",
        "description": "Dense sampling records what an animation system actually evaluated, but it produces a poor final representation: every sampled frame can become a key, edit handles become noisy, and animated vector paths remain hard to adjust. Existing reducers usually treat the two axes separately: animation-curve ",
        "title_cn": "bbsolver ：关键定时和拓扑一致矢量路径的统一误差有界时空优化求解器"
      },
      {
        "title": "Sambe Approach to Floquet-Lindblad Open Quantum Systems",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09727v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T16:50:52Z",
        "description": "We study driven and open quantum systems described by a time-periodic Lindblad master equation. In closed systems, the stroboscopic dynamics can always be described by an effective time-independent Floquet Hamiltonian; this idea is the basis of Floquet engineering. However, in the presence of dissip",
        "title_cn": "Floquet-Lindblad开放量子系统的Sambe方法"
      },
      {
        "title": "NEXUS: Abundance, Environments, and Spectral Diversity of Little Red Dots from the NIRSpec MSA Sample",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09721v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T16:45:43Z",
        "description": "We present a comprehensive study of Little Red Dots (LRDs) at 2.3 90%) of the spectroscopically confirmed LRDs have robust broad-line detection. Our spectroscopic sample of 36 LRDs displays the full range of spectral diversity of LRDs. It includes objects with extreme Balmer breaks similar to the LR",
        "title_cn": "NEXUS ：来自NIRSpec MSA样本的小红点的丰度、环境和光谱多样性"
      },
      {
        "title": "Safe Polytope-in-Polytope Motion Planning and Control with Control Barrier Functions",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09719v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-06-08T16:44:28Z",
        "description": "Autonomous mobile robots operating in tight environments require motion planning frameworks that account for the physical footprint of the robot. Simplifying the geometry to a point or a circle is conservative and discards information needed to successfully and safely traverse narrow passages. This ",
        "title_cn": "具有控制屏障功能的安全Polytope-in-Polytope运动规划和控制"
      }
    ],
    "source": "arXiv",
    "updated": "2026-06-09 06:03 UTC"
